        <definition>std::shared_ptr&lt; uint8_t &gt; ONNX_LIGHT_NAMESPACE::utils::mmap_file_as_shared_ptr</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;file_path, int64_t file_size)</argsstring>
        <name>mmap_file_as_shared_ptr</name>
        <qualifiedname>ONNX_LIGHT_NAMESPACE::utils::mmap_file_as_shared_ptr</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>file_path</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int64_t</type>
          <declname>file_size</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Maps an entire file into read-only virtual memory and returns a shared_ptr&lt;uint8_t&gt; whose deleter unmaps the region. On POSIX, mmap(MAP_PRIVATE|PROT_READ) is used; on Windows, CreateFileMapping + MapViewOfFile. Returns an empty shared_ptr when <emphasis>file_size</emphasis> is 0. The mapped base address is page-aligned and therefore satisfies any typical tensor alignment requirement (16 / 32 / 64 bytes) when combined with an aligned file offset. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
